# 5. USER ROLES AND ACCESS CONTROL

Implement four distinct user roles.

### A. Customer

Customers must be able to:
- Register and log in.
- Manage personal profiles.
- Browse sports.
- Search sports facilities.
- Filter facilities.
- View facility information.
- Check available time slots.
- Book facilities.
- Book trainers.
- Make payments.
- View booking confirmations.
- Cancel bookings.
- Reschedule bookings.
- View booking history.
- Submit ratings and reviews.
- Manage preferences.
- Receive notifications.

### B. Trainer

Trainers must be able to:
- Register or access an authorized trainer account.
- Create and manage trainer profiles.
- Add experience and certifications.
- Specify sports expertise.
- Set session pricing.
- Manage availability.
- View upcoming sessions.
- Accept or manage session bookings.
- Update session status.
- View booking history.

### C. Facility Owner

Facility owners must be able to:
- Add sports facilities.
- Upload facility images.
- Specify sports supported.
- Add descriptions and locations.
- Set booking prices.
- Define operating hours.
- Manage available time slots.
- View facility bookings.
- Manage reservations.
- Update facility information.
- View facility-related statistics.

### D. Administrator

Administrators must have a dedicated administrative dashboard.

Admin functionalities:
- Manage registered customers.
- Manage trainer accounts.
- Approve or reject trainer profiles.
- Manage facility owners.
- Add, update, and remove sports.
- Manage sports facilities.
- Monitor all bookings.
- Monitor payment records.
- Manage cancellations.
- Handle reported issues.
- Moderate reviews.
- View system analytics.
- Monitor platform activity.

Implement role-based access control (RBAC) at both the frontend and backend levels.

A customer must never be able to access administrator or facility-owner operations by changing a URL.

