# 7. NON-FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS

All ten non-functional requirements from the SDF laboratory manual must be addressed.

### NFR1 – Performance
The application should respond to normal user requests within approximately three seconds under normal operating conditions.

Optimize queries, images, components, and loading behavior.

### NFR2 – Security
Implement:
- Secure password handling.
- Authentication.
- Role-based authorization.
- Server-side input validation.
- Protected API routes.
- Database access policies.
- Secure environment variables.
- Protection against unauthorized access.

### NFR3 – Availability
Prepare the application for reliable 24/7 availability, subject to hosting-provider availability and planned maintenance.

### NFR4 – Usability
Maintain an intuitive interface for customers, trainers, facility owners, and administrators.

### NFR5 – Scalability
Use modular architecture and an appropriately structured relational database to support increasing users, facilities, trainers, and bookings.

### NFR6 – Reliability
Prevent double booking and ensure consistent booking and payment statuses.

### NFR7 – Maintainability
Use reusable components, modular code, clear naming conventions, and maintainable project architecture.

### NFR8 – Compatibility
Ensure compatibility with commonly used desktop and mobile browsers.

### NFR9 – Data Integrity
Maintain consistent relationships between customers, trainers, facilities, bookings, payments, and sessions.

### NFR10 – Backup and Recovery
Document and configure database backup and recovery procedures appropriate to the selected hosting plan.

